    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d66">

                <pb facs="0172" n="62" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg62"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">39011163 Christian and Missionary
                    Alliance/1</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Egypt</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Winship</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-01-05"><hi rendition="#italic">January 5,
                        1928</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received February 3.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 153</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to enclose herewith an
                    original letter in Arabic, with translation, addressed to this Legation by the
                    Department for Foreign Affairs of the Government of the Hedjaz and Nejd, calling
                    attention to the danger to travelers entering that country without permits.</p>
                <p>This letter has been acknowledged, and I am also bringing the facts contained
                    therein to the attention of the Consular officers in Egypt, Palestine, and
                    Syria.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">North Winship</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d66-a1.xml" xpointer="d66-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
